"""Two school composites, in the owner's combo architecture. Owner's first person in the frame; second person in the stories.
Each section becomes its own page run in build.py. Paragraph markup: plain strings; '*x*' = italic."""

COVER = {
    "eyebrow": "Combinations · for people who work in schools",
    "title": "Two machines, one building",
    "lede": ("Two stories from inside a school. In both, the school psychologist is good at the job, and so is everyone around him. "
             "Nobody lies. Nobody is careless. Every sentence anyone says is true. And in both, a real person still pays a real cost."),
    "body": ("I wrote these to show what a combination is: a set of ordinary steps, in a particular order, where each step makes the next one feel reasonable. "
             "Each story is followed by its full architecture: the tactics in order, why the order matters, why the system produces that order in the first place, "
             "how the same machine runs in an institution and across a society, how to recognise it, and how to start breaking it."),
    "note": "Composites. They describe a design, not anyone's intent, and not every school or every year.",
}

