            "\"I've tried everything I have.\" She counts on her fingers, and you can tell she's counted this list before, alone, at night. \"The seat by my desk. The check-in chart. The break card. I've called his mom four times. She's working nights, she's doing everything she can. I have twenty-eight other kids, three of them still can't read, and I'm by myself in there.\" She looks at the folder in your hand. \"This form is the only thing I can fill out that brings more grown-ups into the room. It's the only door I've got.\"",
