            "In February, Mr. Okafor stops you in the hallway. \"Strange thing,\" he says. \"We had a sub Tuesday. She asked Marcus to take a seat, and before she'd said anything else he goes, 'I'm the behavior kid. I sit in the back.'\" Mr. Okafor gives a small laugh, the kind people give when they're not sure what they just heard.",
            "You don't laugh. You think about a boy who did a block design faster than you could read the instructions, and who has now learned, very efficiently, what the adults around him think he is.",
