        ("Identity Erosion", "*\"I'm the behavior kid. I sit in the back.\"*",
         "He says it before anyone asks. Nobody told him to. A nine-year-old is extremely good at learning what the adults around him believe, and the building has been teaching him, kindly, every day."),
        ("The File Arrives First", "*\"I read his file.\"*",
         "Every new adult meets the paper before the boy, because files are built to travel and stories aren't. The label walks into each room ahead of him. Each time he acts like the label, the file grows. The loop tightens every time it runs."),
